    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (77.80) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from superior matchups against favorable opposing starters. **Kyle Tucker** continues to be our most reliable engine, drawing a prime spot against McCullers Jr., while **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Houser; despite Houser\u2019s catcher holding a solid pop time, **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s elite lead-off placement makes him a locked-in core play. **Gunnar Henderson** (74.77) also warrants attention; while he faces P\u00e9rez, his propensity for high-leverage production and a helpful matchup against a slower-to-deliver pitcher keeps him near the top of our daily hierarchy, especially given our focus on stealing bases.\n\nWe are hunting upside in the mid-range of our order, where **Andy Pages** (66.49) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.13) offer significant value. **Sam Antonacci** specifically benefits from an elite xwOBA profile and a soft landing against Ure\u00f1a, while **Andy Pages** remains a high-floor start thanks to a favorable dynamic platoon. The most difficult personnel decision of the day involved **Nolan Schanuel**, who finished with a respectable 59.14 score. While **Nolan Schanuel** was the primary candidate to displace the lower-scoring **Heliot Ramos** (45.74), the current lineup optimization favored keeping **Heliot Ramos** at the top of the order to capitalize on potential volume, despite the risk associated with his difficult matchup against Rodriguez.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, particularly for **Jacob Wilson** (46.90), who faces the toughest assignment of the day in Wheeler. While we have kept him in the lineup to maximize position flexibility, his score is suppressed significantly by Wheeler\u2019s elite stuff, leaving his output as a \"marginal\" play at best. We are also keeping a close eye on the weather and official lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, whose base projection is slightly tempered by a difficult matchup against Woo. Should late-breaking news shift the environment, we are prepared to pivot from our current starters, but as of this morning, our focus remains on leveraging the speed and on-base skills of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Sam Antonacci** to close the gap in our scarcest categories.",
